---
// A short red brush mark under a section title. The wipe-on reveal runs when the heading before it gets `.in`
// (site.js adds it as the heading scrolls into view); see `.mark` in site.css. Needs <BrushMarkDefs /> once on the page.
// This <use> is the no-JS fallback: home.js swaps each one for a canvas with its own take of the stroke, so the
// titles on a page do not repeat the same mark.
---

<svg class="mark" aria-hidden="true">
  <use href="#rk-mark"></use>
</svg>
